    "body": "## Motivation\n\nFixes #45481. Concurrent arrivals can split Qwen3.5's remaining 128-token prefill into 105+23 tokens, changing GDN's recurrent-state updates despite deterministic inference being enabled.\n\n## Modifications\n\nAlign deterministic SSM prefill chunks to the state-cache chunk size while preserving the attention backend's alignment. Apply this to continuing chunks and the `ignore_eos` admission path as well. Update one existing test double for the added argument; no new test cases.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nReproduced the reported token divergence with Qwen3.5-35B-A3B on 2× H100 (TP1/PP2 + NEXTN). After the fix, all 294 requests across the original and forced repros produced identical 64-token outputs per input. Existing related tests: 56 passed, 56 subtests passed. Formatting and lint checks passed.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo throughput benchmark; this fixes deterministic chunk scheduling.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39563073404](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39563073404)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39563073268](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39563073268)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39563073308](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39563073308)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
