  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "@SouthWest7 FYI, I opened #46525 for #46446, and the two PRs are complementary rather than overlapping. #46525 only changes the GDN backend: under deterministic inference it runs the decode tail of a mixed batch through the decode kernel. The issue's two-request repro needs that, and this PR does not touch it. This PR's chunk alignment covers the concurrency differences that remain with mixed chunk off.\n\nI applied this PR on top of #46525 on 1x H200 (main `d7f832d30a`, Qwen3.5-9B, Triton, deterministic). Client concurrency 1 vs 8, 32 prompts, number of differing outputs:\n\n| | mixed off, radix off | mixed on, radix off | mixed on, radix on |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| #46525 only | 3/32 | 2/32 | 6/32 |\n| #46525 + this PR | 0/32 | 0/32 | 1/32 |\n\nAlso, this PR now conflicts with `8252e3af63` (#41701) in `schedule_policy.py`, which wraps both cut sites in `floor_chunked_tokens`. For the runs above I kept this PR's side of both hunks, which is equivalent without DCP.\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-26T06:29:59Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/45545#issuecomment-6409748966",
      "id": 6409748966,
